The O3DE lighting investigation's overlay
=========================================

What the investigation draws over the room, from what its code computes (src/o3de/lighting/script.rs): the
light's attenuation radius and falloff, and at the inspected point the vectors the BRDF is a function of, its
lobes, and the directions the specular prefilter samples.
The lab draws it over each frame (lab/src/script/runtime.rs).

$[Import* std]
$[Import* render_lab_runtime]
$[Import* o3de_lighting_values]
$[Import* o3de_lighting_natives]

The colours of the light, the half vector, and the two lobes (src/o3de/lighting/demos.rs).
$[# _light "#ffd98a"]
$[# _half "#b49cff"]
$[# _specular "#ff8fc8"]
$[# _diffuse "#8fe3a0"]

The vectors at the inspected point, in the order `vectorsShown` grows them: N, then L and H while the light is
on, V, and R in the IBL demonstration.
$[# {_shown i}
    [# n {named "N" {.normal i} normalColor}]
    [# v {named "V" {.toView i} viewColor}]
    [# lit {!if {.lightOn i}
        {' n {named "L" {.toLight i} _light} v {named "H" {.half i} _half}}
        {' n v}}]
    {!if {= {demo} "ibl"} {append lit {' {named "R" {.reflect i} reflectedColor}}} lit}]

The inspected point and its vectors (`vectors` fades them, `vectorsShown` grows them one by one), a dashed line
to the light once L is out, and the observer the readout sees the point from, when it has one.
$[# {_vectors i alpha}
    [# p {.point i}]
    [# count {max {vectorsShown} 0.0}]
    [# toLight {!if {!and {.lightOn i} {> count 1.0}}
        {' {dashed p {.lightAt i} _light {* alpha 0.5} 1.5}}
        {'}}]
    [# seen {vec3 {observerX} {observerY} {observerZ}}]
    [# observed {!if {> {observer} 0.5}
        {'
            {point seen 9.0 viewColor alpha}
            {dashed p seen viewColor {* alpha 0.5} 1.5}
            {labelText seen {textKey "demos.observer"} viewColor}}
        {'}}]
    {flatten {'
        {' {point p 8.0 selectedColor alpha}}
        {grownArrows p {_shown i} 0.5 alpha 4.0 count}
        toLight
        observed}}]

The specular and diffuse lobes for an outgoing direction swept through the plane of N and L, horizon to horizon,
each on its own scale (`brdfTerms`), and the mirror direction of L, where a smooth surface's lobe peaks.
$[# {_lobes i alpha}
    [# n {.normal i}]
    [# at {.surface i}]
    [# dirs {sweep n {inPlane n {.toLight i}} 90}]
    [# terms {brdfTerms dirs}]
    {flatten {'
        {lobeLine at dirs
            {.specular terms}
            _specular
            0.8
            alpha
            3.0
            {some {textKey "demos.specular_lobe"}}}
        {lobeLine at dirs {.diffuse terms} _diffuse 0.4 alpha 3.0 none}
        {'
            {dashed at
                {vadd at {vscale {mirror n {.toLight i}} 0.65}}
                _specular
                {* alpha 0.6}
                1.5}}}}]

Three great circles around the light at its attenuation radius, and the circle where that sphere meets the floor.
$[# {_circle a b r c} {map
    {range 0 97}
    {^ {k}
        [# t {* {/ {float k} 96.0} {* 2.0 pi}}]
        {vadd c {vscale {vadd {vscale a {cos t}} {vscale b {sin t}}} r}}}}]
$[# {_radius i alpha}
    [# c {.lightAt i}]
    [# r {.lightRadius i}]
    [# x {vec3 1.0 0.0 0.0}]
    [# y {vec3 0.0 1.0 0.0}]
    [# z {vec3 0.0 0.0 1.0}]
    [# rings {flatten {map
        {' {pair x y} {pair y z} {pair x z}}
        {^ {p} {polyline {_circle {.first p} {.second p} r c} _light {* alpha 0.35} 1.5}}}}]
    [# floor {!if {< {.y c} r}
        {polyline
            {_circle x z {sqrt {- {* r r} {* {.y c} {.y c}}}} {vec3 {.x c} 0.005 {.z c}}}
            _light
            {* alpha 0.9}
            3.0}
        {'}}]
    {append rings floor}]

The illuminance on the floor along +x from below the light, as a curve standing on the floor: inverse-square
alone (dashed) and with SimplePointLight's radius attenuation (solid), both on one scale (`falloffCurve`).
$[# {_falloff i alpha}
    [# l {.lightAt i}]
    [# foot {vec3 {.x l} 0.0 {.z l}}]
    [# xs {map {range 0 121} {^ {k} {* 3.0 {/ {float k} 120.0}}}}]
    [# f {falloffCurve xs}]
    [# {at x v} {vadd foot {vec3 x {* 1.2 {min v 1.4}} 0.0}}]
    [# plain {map {zip xs {.plain f}} {^ {e} {at {.first e} {.second e}}}}]
    [# attenuated {map {zip xs {.attenuated f}} {^ {e} {at {.first e} {.second e}}}}]
    [# dashes {map
        {zip plain {tail plain}}
        {^ {e} {dashed {.first e} {.second e} textDimColor {* alpha 0.8} 2.0}}}]
    {flatten {'
        {' {arrow foot {vadd foot {vec3 3.0 0.0 0.0}} textFaintColor {* alpha 0.6} 1.5}}
        dashes
        {polyline attenuated _light alpha 3.5}
        {'
            {label {nth plain 40} "I / d²" textDimColor}
            {label {nth attenuated 70} "I / d² · (1 − (d²/r²)²)²" _light}}}}]

The first `ggxSamples` of the 256 directions the specular prefilter samples for a texel along R, brighter the
closer to R.
$[# {_ggx i count}
    [# r {.reflect i}]
    [# p {.surface i}]
    {flatten {map
        {ggxDirections count}
        {^ {l}
            [# w {vdot r l}]
            {!if {> w 0.0}
                {' {segment p {vadd p {vscale l 0.55}} _specular {+ 0.25 {* 0.6 w}} 1.5}}
                {'}}}}}]

$[# {_draw i}
    [# samples {clamp {round {ggxSamples}} 0 256}]
    {flatten {'
        {!if {> {radius} 0.0} {_radius i {radius}} {'}}
        {!if {> {falloff} 0.0} {_falloff i {falloff}} {'}}
        {!if {> {vectors} 0.0} {_vectors i {vectors}} {'}}
        {!if {> {lobe} 0.0} {_lobes i {lobe}} {'}}
        {!if {> samples 0} {_ggx i samples} {'}}}}]

The overlay: nothing while the unfolded cubemap covers the room.
$[# overlay {: {^ {t} {!if {> {probeCubemap} 0.5} {'} {_draw {inspected}}}} Overlay}]
